Touchscreen gestures for niri 26.04, from niri-wm/niri#3180: three fingers
move the view and the workspaces, four open and close the overview, as the
touchpad's do. Beyond #3180, they move as a screen's should: the content
follows the fingers, as far as they move, however many there are. And a
third finger cancels the touches the client already had, and the client
sees nothing more until every finger has lifted, so a swipe never reaches
it as a tap or as touches left unfinished.

